**Depends on #1380** (the `Resource` type).

## Problem

`auth.Client` satisfies `remote.Client`, whose whole surface is `Do(*http.Request)` (`registry/remote/repository.go:85`). The request is therefore the only channel from caller to auth layer. For the auth layer to resolve a credential for `example.com/myspace` rather than just `example.com`, it has to know the repository path — and today it never computes one.

## Proposal

In `Client.Do`, derive a `Resource` from the request URL: strip a leading `/v2/`, then split at the **rightmost** `/manifests/`, `/blobs/`, `/tags/list`, or `/referrers/`. What remains is the repository path.

```
/v2/myspace/app/manifests/v1        -> {Host: h, Path: "myspace/app"}
/v2/myspace/app/blobs/sha256:...    -> {Host: h, Path: "myspace/app"}
/v2/myspace/app/tags/list           -> {Host: h, Path: "myspace/app"}
/v2/                                -> {Host: h, Path: ""}
/some/other/path                    -> {Host: h, Path: ""}
```

Rightmost, because `<name>` may itself contain a segment called `blobs` or `manifests`.

